# Documentation

The customer guide is written. The same pages are what `docs.autoconnecto.in` and the in-app Documentation menu show. Swagger stays the generated API reference. Builder notes stay in git.

## On every customer-visible change

Do this in the same change, before you call the work done:

1. Update the page in `docs/docs/` that explains the screen or behavior. Add the path to `docs/customer-pages.json` if it is a new page. Keep `docs/CONTENTS.md` in step with that list.
2. Where the screen is what the page explains, add a screenshot under `docs/docs/public/images/<section>/` and embed it. Use the screen you actually changed. Do not draw a fake screenshot, and do not include a secret, a token, or a live alarm you were not asked to touch.
3. If the public claim changed (a feature exists, a price, a setup step), update `website/` in the same change. Do not put another product’s name on the website or in the platform.

A scanner does not write these pages. `backend/scripts/publish-written-docs.mjs` copies `docs/customer-pages.json` into the in-app bundle. The HTTP generate endpoints refuse. Swagger in the app stays.

## Product facts the pages must keep

- Telemetry and device attributes are stored without a save node. Drop is the only way a reading is not stored.
- Profile alarm rules and a chain alarm both run. Say so when both exist.
- Quiet hours and Monday energy mail stay off unless he asked to turn them on.
- Camera, WhatsApp, ISO 27001, and an on-prem install stay out of the docs until a contract asks for them.

## Builder notes

A transport or contract change still updates `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `backend/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `backend/ENVIRONMENT.md`, `frontend/WIDGET_ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `sdk/TRANSPORT_ARCHITECTURE.md` when that file is the contract. Those files are not the customer guide.

## Publish

Pushing `autoconnecto-docs` `main` publishes the public site and dispatches `docs-changed` so the in-app menu is the same pages. Do not deploy unless he asks. A backend or frontend push does not rebuild the guide.
